// @expect-error Override of 'count' returns 'int', but the 'count' declared in 'Base' returns 'long', and the two are held differently at run time. An override may narrow a class, interface, array, string, function or handle reference, where both spellings are one pointer, but not a number and not a nullable value type. Return 'long'.
// @expect-error Override of 'scale' returns 'float', but the 'scale' declared in 'Base' returns 'double', and the two are held differently at run time. An override may narrow a class, interface, array, string, function or handle reference, where both spellings are one pointer, but not a number and not a nullable value type. Return 'double'.
// @expect-error Override of 'spot' returns 'Point', but the 'spot' declared in 'Base' returns 'Point?', and the two are held differently at run time. An override may narrow a class, interface, array, string, function or handle reference, where both spellings are one pointer, but not a number and not a nullable value type. Return 'Point?'.
// @expect-error Override of 'twice' returns 'Shape?', but the 'twice' declared in 'Base' returns 'Shape??', and the two are held differently at run time. An override may narrow a class, interface, array, string, function or handle reference, where both spellings are one pointer, but not a number and not a nullable value type. Return 'Shape??'.
